      ],
      "extract": "Classical algorithms for approximating partition functions of quantum models that make use of cluster expansions have occurred in two recent papers.1,2 In this paper, we provide a simple and concise exposition of how to construct such algorithms, with the intent of making the technique accessible to a wide audience. A quantum spin system is modelled by a hypergraph G = (X, E). At each vertex x of G, there is a",
